{{define "settings_editor_files.gohtml"}}
{{template "app_start.gohtml" .}}
{{template "editor_page_start.gohtml" .}}
<form method="post" action="/settings/editor/files" id="settings-editor-files">
  <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{.CSRFToken}}">
  <div class="text-secondary small mb-3">While an editor is open, the server watches its open tabs and unfolded folders. A file that changed on disk reloads in its tab, one with unsaved changes is marked instead, and the tree follows entries that appear, go or are renamed.</div>
  <div class="mb-3 row">
    <div class="col-12 col-sm-7 col-lg-5">
      <label class="form-label" for="editor-file-poll">Check the disk every</label>
      <div class="input-group">
        <input class="form-control" type="number" id="editor-file-poll" name="file_poll_seconds" min="0" max="60" step="1" value="{{.FilePollSeconds}}">
        <span class="input-group-text">seconds</span>
      </div>
      <div class="form-text">Runs only while an editor of that project is open. Zero switches it off; the refresh button above the file tree still reads the tree. Separate from the git interval on the Git tab: one round here is a stat per watched path, a git status walks the whole working copy.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Save</button>
</form>
{{template "editor_page_end.gohtml"}}
{{template "app_end.gohtml" .}}
{{end}}
